// WIRED 16 August 2026, task #116, Phase B.
//
// ── THIS SCREEN WAS NOT MERELY UNWIRED. IT WAS UNTRUE. ───────────────────
//
// What it showed before, on every property, regardless of anything:
//
//   * "Visa ending in 4242 · Expires 12/26" with a tick beside it, under a
//     "Payment method" heading with a "Change" link. There is no saved card
//     anywhere in GoOuts. 4242 is Stripe's test card number.
//   * A "Confirm and pay" button with `onPressed: () {}`.
//   * "Secure payment" and "SSL Encrypted" badges beneath it.
//   * "Your deposit is a temporary hold on your card, released within forty
//     eight hours of departure." No card is held. Nothing is released.
//   * £112 × 2 nights, £224, £30 cleaning, £15 service, £269 total — fixed
//     numbers unrelated to the property being booked.
//
// A guest reading that screen would reasonably believe they had just been
// charged £269 to a Visa. Nothing was taken, and nothing could have been:
// there is no payment integration in this product.
//
// stay_booking_service already carried the flag for this, and its comment says
// what was needed plainly:
//
//     /// There is no payment integration. Always false today. A checkout
//     /// screen that says "Pay now" while this is false is lying to the guest.
//     final bool paymentAvailable;
//
// The flag was built. This screen never read it. So the fix is not new
// plumbing — it is using what the service already says about itself.
//
// ── WHAT IT DOES NOW ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Calls getStayQuote for the real listing, dates and party size, and shows
// what comes back. No payment section. The button reads "Request to book" or
// "Confirm booking" depending on the host's booking mode, never "pay". The
// notice explains, in the guest's own terms, that nothing is charged now and
// that the hold expires after 48 hours — which is the server's actual
// behaviour, not a reassurance invented for the screen.
//
// WHEN PAYMENTS ARE BUILT: the quote's paymentAvailable flips true and the
// payment section belongs here. Restore it then, with a real card. Not before.
import 'dart:math';

import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import 'package:google_fonts/google_fonts.dart';

import '../models/stay_booking_request.dart';
import '../models/stay_enums.dart';
import '../models/stay_listing.dart';
import '../services/stay_booking_service.dart';
import '../services/stay_listing_service.dart';
import '../stay_routes.dart';
